<title>USA: First Union may buy up to 25 mln shares.</title>
<headline>First Union may buy up to 25 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLOTTE, N.C. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Union Corp said Monday that it may repurchase up to 25 million shares of its outstanding common shares.</p>
<p>The bank holding company said these shares would include a number equal to 2.6 million shares issued in its December 11 acquisition of Keystone Investments Inc, which it said should not affect year-end earnings.</p>
<p>The company said it continues to expect 1996 earnings to be $6.31 per share, excluding merger-related charges in the first quarter and special federal insurance assessments.  </p>
<p>The company said it had 287.3 million common shares outstanding as of December 31.</p>
